    description: "FOUND BY MEASUREMENT 0019, 2026-09-08. The c twin of WI-gotun (java), filed\nafter PRICING THE REMEDY rather than assuming it.\n\nTHE FACT. `registered_def_use_languages()` returns exactly\n`go, javascript, python, rust, typescript`. c has no def/use extractor, and\nunlike java it has no CFG mapping either: `verify-claims --json` names FOUR\nblockers for c (`cfg_mapping`, `atomic_statement`, `def_use_extractor`,\n`ddg_spec`) against java's three, with `catalog_sinks: 54`,\n`catalog_sources: 39`, `catalog_sanitizers: 0`. Every c taint finding is\ntherefore labelled `structural`, uniformly, because that is the only branch\nreachable.\n\nWHAT IT COSTS, MEASURED, AND IT IS NOT WHAT MEASUREMENT 0019 FIRST IMPLIED.\nSix fixtures, three flow shapes x c and python, each a separate repo and a\nseparate run so every verdict is attributable\n(`~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/c_defuse_09082026/RESULT.md`):\n\n  fixture            lang    shape                  method       removed  verdict\n  fx_realflow        c       result -> sink         structural   0        violated\n  fx_colocated       c       co-located, no flow    structural   0        violated\n  fx_c_discard       c       discarded at source    structural   0        violated\n  fx_py_realflow     python  result -> sink         ddg          0        violated\n  fx_py_colocated    python  co-located, no flow    ddg_mixed    0        violated\n  fx_py_discard      python  discarded at source    structural   0        violated\n\nALL SIX REPORT ONE FINDING AND ONE VIOLATED CLAIM, and\n`flows_removed_by_walk` is 0 IN ALL SIX -- PYTHON INCLUDED. The two c\nfixtures that differ in whether a real dependence exists produced\nbyte-identical JSON apart from line numbers.\n\nSO THE EXTRACTOR DOES NOT REMOVE FALSE POSITIVES. It changes the METHOD\nLABEL and not the population. `dataflow_scope`'s module docstring states the\nmechanism: the walk only ever SUBTRACTS and removes only on `unconfirmed`;\n`escaped` is ignorance and removes nothing. That docstring records the\nremoval class as measured-EMPTY on measurement 0019's own 11-repo cohort\n(0 unconfirmed / 14 escaped / 139 not_attempted). It activates as escape\nsites close -- INV-busis, which the arc schedules last as capacity work.\n\nMeasurement 0019's own table carried the counter-evidence before anyone drew\nit: the vault false positive is in `go`, WHICH HAS AN EXTRACTOR, labelled\n`ddg_mixed`. 0019 has been amended in place with this correction.\n\nWHAT THE GAP THEREFORE COSTS IS TRIAGE, NOT PRECISION. In python a reader\nseparates `ddg` (dependence proven) from `ddg_mixed` (function had a DDG,\nthis path unproven) from `structural` (the walk had nothing to say). In c the\nlabel carries ZERO BITS, and a c reader filtering on\n`analysis_method == \"ddg\"` gets an empty set, always. On 0019's cohort that\nis 5 findings a reader cannot triage; on a c-heavy repo it is every finding.\n\nTHE \"OR DECLARE BLIND\" HALF IS ALREADY SHIPPED, exactly as for java, and this\nitem does not reopen it: the per-language `dataflow_coverage` row names all\nfour blockers machine-readably on every run. The arc's \"ship the extractor or\na dated declared blindness; silence stays banned\" obligation is met on the\nblindness branch without building anything.\n\nRANKED BELOW ITS JAVA TWIN, ON TWO MEASURED AXES. (1) c needs FOUR blockers\nclosed to java's three -- there is no `cfg_nodes/c.yaml`, so c needs the CFG\nhalf java already has. (2) The same-function sanitizer arm\n(`if adjudicated and barrier_sites:`) requires DDG confirmation, and\nWI-gotun's 2026-08-25 amendment bounded java's benefit by java's ONE\nsanitizer row; c has ZERO, so that entire benefit is exactly zero for c until\nc sanitizer rows exist. More work, strictly less payoff.\n\nSCOPE IF BUILT: `cfg_nodes/c.yaml` (conditional / loop / switch / goto),\nCDefUseExtractor (declaration, assignment_expression, parameter bindings,\ncompound assignment, address-of as a def-escape), `atomic_statement` in\nc.yaml, a registered LanguageDdgSpec, and c added to\nEXPECTED_DEF_USE_LANGUAGES in the same PR so `test_ddg_language_wiring` stops\nsilently quantifying over the current set.\n\nRECOMMENDATION: DO NOT BUILD NOW. Its function today is to be the named,\ndated home for \"c findings are uniformly structural\", so the next reader of a\nlow c precision number finds the cause instead of re-deriving it. Reconsider\nwhen either (a) c sanitizer rows exist, or (b) INV-busis closes escape sites\nfar enough that the refutation class stops being empty -- at which point the\nbenefit changes KIND, from labelling to removal, and this item should be\nre-ranked rather than re-argued.\n\nNOT ESTABLISHED, stated so the gap is visible: whether c's false-positive\nconcentration in 0019 is caused by the analyzer at all. The competing\nexplanation is a CORPUS property -- c code co-locating resolver calls with\n`printf` more often than python co-locates them with `subprocess` -- and this\ncohort does not separate the two."  # 25a7
